// (0.18.1) Incremental rebuilds: the code cache (T8 of
// docs/design/contracts-verification.md; docs/optimizer.md, "0.18.1:
// incremental rebuilds"). A task of middle::parallel whose inputs are the
// same as in an earlier build takes that build's outputs instead of
// running: -O2's cleanup and scalar pipeline of a function (its IR), -O2's
// components (their functions' optimized IR and facts) and every
// function's emission (its text), at -O1 and -O2.
//
// An entry is found by its key: the compiler, the options and the
// program's types (env), the task's functions by symbol, their IR as the
// task receives it (hash::ir_hash) and what the program knows of them
// (own_fp). It holds what the task read of other functions while it ran
// (a verifying trace): each read is recorded when it is made (cc_note,
// from the accessors: the callee of a call, its readiness, size,
// attributes, call flags, deciders and IR) with the value read, and the
// entry is used only when every one reads the same now. Two reads of the
// program record the answer, not the value: the inlining budget (whether
// the program's size plus a growth is within it) and a callee's calls
// left (whether one). The outputs name strings, symbols, functions and
// constant data by what they are (snapshot::Rel), mapped to this build's
// ids when used.
//
// A task that reads something the trace cannot hold (IR whose hash is not
// known) is poisoned: it runs and nothing is stored. The output with the
// cache is the same as without, byte for byte (tests/incremental.sh).

pub mod hash;
pub mod snapshot;
pub mod pack;

